{
  "data": {
    "id": 1122274,
    "name": "Garlic Scapes",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Garlic scapes are the&nbsp;edible, curly flower stalks of hardneck garlic, harvested in late spring/early summer for a milder, sweeter garlic flavor than raw cloves, with a texture like asparagus or green beans.&nbsp;They are versatile and can be eaten raw (in pesto), sautéed, grilled, roasted, or blended into soups and sauces, often used as a substitute for garlic or scallions.&nbsp;To prepare, trim the woody ends and the flower bud, then cook them until tender, or use them raw in pesto.&nbsp;</span><br><br></p>",
